<BaseLayout
  title="Download Core-Geth for Ethereum Classic: Linux, macOS, Windows"
  crumb="Downloads"
  description="Download Core-Geth for Linux, macOS, Windows, Arm or Docker, or build from source. Every release carries a checksum and a build attestation you can verify."
  path="/downloads/"
>
  <PageHero label="Core-Geth downloads" title="Get the Core-Geth client." em="Core-Geth">
    <p class="lede">
      Download a release for Linux, macOS or Windows, run it as a container, or build the client
      from source. Every archive and image is published with a checksum and a build attestation, so
      you can confirm what you downloaded before you run it.
    </p>
    <div class="downloads__actions">
      <a class="button button--primary" href={REPO.latestUrl}>
        The latest release
      </a>
      <a class="button" href={DOCS.installation.href}>
        Installation guide
      </a>
    </div>
    {downloads && (
      <p class="downloads__meta">
        {`Latest release ${downloads.tag}, published ${formatAsOf(downloads.published)}. `}
        <a href={downloads.notes}>Release notes</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href={REPO.releasesUrl}>All releases</a>
      </p>
    )}
  </PageHero>

  <section class="band band--surface" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="container downloads__install">
      <SectionHead
        id="install-title"
        label="Install Core-Geth"
        title="How to download, install, and run the Core-Geth client"
        em="download, install, and run"
      >
        <p class="lede">
          Each block takes the build most machines need: the x86-64 archive on Linux, Apple Silicon
          on macOS, the published image for containers. Check an archive against its checksum and
          its build attestation before you run it: <a href="#verify">both commands</a> are at the
          foot of this page.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          {`Every archive and image on this page is from the latest ${RECOMMENDED_LINE} release. If you are replacing a `}
          <InlineCode text={EXPOSED_LINE} />
          {` node, that node needs a new P2P key before it starts again: `}
          <a href={`#${UPGRADE_ANCHOR}`}>{`moving a ${EXPOSED_LINE} node`}</a>
          {` has the commands.`}
        </p>
      </SectionHead>
      <PlatformTabs legend="Choose your platform" panels={PANELS}>
        <p class="panel__note" slot="before-linux">
          The x86-64 and Arm64 archives need glibc 2.17 or newer, which is RHEL 7, CentOS 7 and
          anything more recent; the 32-bit Arm archives need glibc 2.28 or newer. The{" "}
          <a href={`${DOCS.releaseReport.href}#archives`}>release report</a> lists every archive and
          its platform.
        </p>
        <Fragment slot="before-source">
          <a class="source-repo" href={REPO.url}>
            github.com/{REPO.slug.split("/")[0]}/<wbr />
            {REPO.slug.split("/")[1]}
          </a>
          <p class="panel__note">
            Each tab starts from a machine with none of the build tools: it installs them, checks
            each one's version, and builds the <code>main</code> branch.
          </p>
          <PlatformTabs
            legend="Choose your platform for building from source"
            panels={SOURCE_PANELS}
            prefix="source-"
            nested
          />
        </Fragment>
        <ReleaseFiles slot="after-linux" group={groupFor("linux")} />
        <ReleaseFiles slot="after-macos" group={groupFor("macos")} />
        <ReleaseFiles slot="after-windows" group={groupFor("windows")} />
        <ReleaseFiles slot="after-containers" group={groupFor("containers")} />
      </PlatformTabs>

      <p class="downloads__note">
        An <code>alltools</code> archive is the same client with the rest of the tools beside it:{" "}
        <code>abigen</code>, <code>clef</code>, <code>evm</code>, <code>rlpdump</code> and the
        others. To run a node, take the plain archive.
      </p>
    </div>
