      <SectionHead
        id="verify-title"
        label="Verify a Core-Geth download"
        title="Verify what you downloaded"
        em="Verify"
        size="medium"
      >
        <p class="lede">
          The checksum says the file arrived intact. The attestation says which workflow built it,
          from which commit.
        </p>
      </SectionHead>
      <PlatformTabs
        legend="Choose your platform for checking a download"
        panels={VERIFY_PANELS}
        prefix="verify-"
      >
        <PlatformTabs
          slot="before-source"
          legend="Choose your platform for checking a build from source"
          panels={VERIFY_SOURCE_PANELS}
          prefix="verify-source-"
          nested
        />
      </PlatformTabs>
      <div class="downloads__group">
        <h3>What every release carries</h3>
        <ul class="plain" role="list">
          <li>
            <strong>A checksum beside every file.</strong> A <code>.sha256</code> is published with
            each archive and each image tarball.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A build attestation on every archive and image.</strong> It is minted against a
            short-lived certificate issued to the workflow run itself, and records which workflow,
            at which commit, produced the file, so each one traces to the run that built it rather
            than resting on anyone's word.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Provenance for the container images.</strong> Recorded for the published image
            index and for each image tarball.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          On a first run Windows names the publisher as unknown, and macOS blocks a downloaded
          binary until it is allowed. The <a href={DOCS.installation.href}>installation guide</a>{" "}
          says how to check an archive and proceed.
        </p>
        <a class="more" href={`${DOCS_URL}audits/2026-09-release-pipeline/`}>
          <ArrowText text="How the release artifacts are built and checked" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

